Rejected in M14 (docs/PERFORMANCE.md 11.3, R1): skip a resolve whose source EDRAM data and destination are
unchanged since the same resolve last copied them. Render targets carry a contents generation, bumped by every draw
that writes them (colour always, depth when z or stencil writes are on) and by ownership transfers; a resolve
records its registers and its sources' generations, and is skipped when both match and no CPU or GPU write touched
its destination since (a global shared memory watch, plus memory export draws). Correct (identical captures at 1440p
and 4K, no new validation messages) and about 10 % of 4K resolves were skipped, but GPU time and frame rate did not
move measurably (4K GPU 7.0 vs 6.9 ms per frame, 3 reps each), so it was not kept. Applies on top of SDK patches
0001-0017 as of M14 (not maintained).
